  "description": "PymooSampler for OptunaSharp — a native OptunaSharp BaseSampler that drives the real pymoo (the multi-objective evolutionary-optimization library) in-process via Python.NET (pythonnet). One sampler exposes pymoo's whole multi-objective algorithm zoo — NSGA-II, NSGA-III, R-NSGA-II, R-NSGA-III, U-NSGA-III, AGE-MOEA, AGE-MOEA-2, RVEA, SMS-EMOA, SPEA2, C-TAEA — through a pythonnet-free PymooAlgorithm enum. The Optuna side (study, storage, ask/tell, search space) is native OptunaSharp; the operators, reference-direction machinery and HV/decomposition survival are genuine pymoo, reconstructed from the study's completed trials and driven through pymoo's native ask()/tell() — the same reconstruct-from-trials bridge as OptunaSharp.Interop.PyCma / .BoTorch. Configurable through PymooAlgorithmOptions: SBX crossover + PM mutation, duplicate elimination, RVEA alpha/adapt_freq, R-NSGA weights/mu/epsilon, and Das-Dennis / Riesz-energy reference directions. Supports constrained optimization (pymoo's G ≤ 0 feasibility, via Trial.SetConstraint or a constraintsFunc) and single-, two- and many-objective studies over Optuna's full parameter space (float/int with log/step, categoricals, dynamic spaces). Beyond Optuna core (Optuna ships only NSGA-II/III), a live-runtime complement to the native AgeMoea2Sampler. Does NOT require any Python glue package — install only `pymoo`. Built on OptunaSharp.Interop.pythonnet. Part of the SciSharp STACK.",
  "iconFile": "optunasharp-icon.png",
